This change removes the postWithAuthor query example from the "One-to-Many" section. This example was valuable as it demonstrated querying from the "many" side (posts) to get the related "one" side (author), a common use case. Its removal makes the documentation for one-to-many relations less complete. Following the tiered documentation structure, detailed reference files should preserve comprehensive examples for clarity.

```suggestion
// Query
const userWithPosts = await db.query.users.findFirst({
  where: eq(users.id, userId),
  with: { posts: true },
});

const postWithAuthor = await db.query.posts.findFirst({
  where: eq(posts.id, postId),
  with: { author: true },
});
```

